---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/privacy.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="JobLens Privacy Policy" description="JobLens privacy policy. No data collected.">
  <main class="privacy-page grid-page">
    <a href="/job-lens/" class="back-link">&larr; JobLens</a>

    <header class="privacy-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: March 12, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>What JobLens Does</h2>
      <p>JobLens is a Chrome extension that helps you filter LinkedIn job listings. It runs entirely in your browser on LinkedIn job pages.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Data Collection</h2>
      <p>JobLens does <strong>not</strong> collect or store any personal data. Specifically:</p>
      <ul class="privacy-list">
        <li>No data sent to external servers by the extension itself</li>
        <li>No cookies set by the extension</li>
        <li>No user accounts or sign-in</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This website (not the extension) uses Google Analytics via Google Tag Manager to understand page visits and button clicks. Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="privacy-link">privacy policy</a> applies to that data. However, <strong>NO PERSONAL IDENTIFIERS</strong> are collected. The analytics data is fully anonymous and is only used to improve the experience, such as underused features may be removed, and popular ones refined, etc.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Local Storage</h2>
      <p>JobLens saves your preferences (skipped companies, skipped title keywords, toggle states) using Chrome's local storage API. This data stays on your device and is never transmitted anywhere.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <ul class="privacy-list">
        <li><strong>storage</strong>: to save your filter preferences locally</li>
        <li><strong>Host permission (linkedin.com/jobs/*)</strong>: to read and annotate job listings on LinkedIn</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>JobLens loads the EB Garamond font from Google Fonts. Google's privacy policy applies to that request. No other third-party services are used.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted here.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Reach out at <a href="/job-lens/" class="privacy-link">kunli.co/job-lens</a>.</p>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
